      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We investigated the effect of abrupt cessation of nifedipine after regular administration (20 mg, four times daily) for 5 weeks in seven patients with stable angina pectoris. A rebound decrease in exercise tolerance and increase of exercise-induced myocardial ischaemia were registered on the first day of nifedipine withdrawal."},
